7592186045417] [17592186198374 #edb/ref 1040 #edb/ref 17592186521963 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186198374 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186198016 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198374 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "b2682751-23e4-5cf2-9a46-82c75765423f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198479 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186199250 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198479 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186199251 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198479 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186199273 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198479 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186199274 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198479 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198479 #edb/ref 1045 "Computing Double Integrals Using a Change of Variables" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198479 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186199250 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198479 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050482 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198479 #edb/ref 1050 1020.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198479 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "8416c2c4-cff0-5744-94c6-6f83c5fc5709" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199007 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186197912 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199007 #edb/ref 1069 "q-82916" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199007 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199007 #edb/ref 1071 "Use a change of variables to evaluate the double integral \n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}(x+2y){e}^{(x+2y)^{2}}\\,dxdy,\n$$\n\nwhere $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 5,\\,0\\le x+2y\\le 1\\}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199007 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f7817742-b76a-5484-9fbf-d87d76ee15f4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199007 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's define a transformation $T$ as follows:\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane to our region $D$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\nTo compute the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dxdy={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(x(u,v),y(u,v))\\,|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\text{ }dudv\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nTo compute the required integral, we proceed as follows:\n\n**Step 1**: Find a suitable change of variables.\n\nThe inequalities that define the region $D,$\n\n$$\n1\\le x\\le 5,\\,0\\le x+2y\\le 1,\n$$\n\nsuggest that we use the change of variables \n\n$$\nu=x\\,\\text{and}\\,v=x+2y.\n$$\n\nThis change of variables gives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}u(x,y) \\\\ v(x,y)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $D$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nOur domain in the $uv$-plane is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,1\\le u\\le 5,\\,0\\le v\\le 1\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & \\text{ }\\text{ }0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}={(\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)})}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 5**: Perform the change of variables, and evaluate the integral:\n\nPerforming the change of variables, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}(x+2y){e}^{(x+2y)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y & ={∬}_{Δ}v{e}^{{v}^{2}}\\,|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={∬}_{Δ}v{e}^{{v}^{2}}\\,|\\frac{1}{2}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{5}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}v{e}^{{v}^{2}}\\,dv]du \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{5}{[\\frac{{e}^{{v}^{2}}}{2}]}_{0}^{1}du \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{1}^{5}(e-1)\\,du \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(e-1)[u]_{1}^{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(e-1)(5-1) \\\\  & =e-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186199250 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186199251 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199250 #edb/ref 1061 26976 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199250 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5a4dcbdc-b666-5ac5-82b5-d1e2d96f958e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199250 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186199451 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199251 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186199273 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199251 #edb/ref 1061 26978 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199251 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "38215948-f2f7-5757-b967-2b0aad077150" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199251 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186198361 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199273 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186199274 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199273 #edb/ref 1061 44170 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199273 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "418d8ff2-cd87-5ef1-b69c-c511c7c5b360" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199273 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186198373 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199274 #edb/ref 1061 44171 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199274 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e9c97e5e-4063-57fd-b261-2a276cea9f27" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199274 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186198374 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
